    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d442">

                <pb facs="0540" n="444" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg444"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Governor Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-07-27"><hi rendition="#italic">July 27,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I beg to thank your excellency for your telegram of yesterday advising me of the
                    steps taken in regard to the lynching of the Italians at Tallulah. The President
                    is gratified and entertains the earnest confidence that nothing will be left
                    undone to promote the ends of justice and to subserve good international
                    relations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
